    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0149_f2ac02ed2057.jpeg\" /><img src=\"assets\\st0149_8e7a510559e3.jpeg\" /></p><p>Grignard reagents add to carbonyl compounds to give primary, secondary, and tertiary alcohols. Reacting a Grignard reagent with an aldehyde gives a secondary alcohol. Reacting a Grignard reagent with a ketone gives a tertiary alcohol.</p>"
